WEBVTT

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.980
I guess I still can't

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.990
get over Shimao...

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.370
So what?!

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.870
That has nothing to do with whether I throw in the towel or not!

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.390
<i>Even if the manager isn't waiting for me in the future,</i>

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.520
<i>I'll do anything to meet her.</i>

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.780
<i>I'll do what I can, and if it doesn't work, it doesn't work.</i>

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.780
<i>Even with that in mind, I have to give it my all...</i>

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.620
<i>since I'd hate to follow in that ghost's footsteps!</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.170
<i>I walk</i>

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.090
<i>and walk</i>

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:10.710
<i>and walk,</i>

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.800
<i>but I still don't run out of breath.</i>

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.590
<i>It feels like no matter how far I go,</i>

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.560
<i>I can just keep moving forward through this bright sunlight.</i>

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:25.940
<i>For the longest time,</i>

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.020
<i>I couldn't do this.</i>

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.860
<i>But it's thanks to Hazuki's young, healthy body.</i>

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.990
<i>This nostalgic sensation that comes through my leg,</i>

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.620
<i>the softness of the muck and the bounce in my step...</i>

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.000
<i>All of this is thanks to Hazuki's body.</i>

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.840
<i>These sensations,</i>

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.260
<i>they're so...</i>

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.050
<i>They're just so...</i>

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:01.760
<i>I can't believe</i>

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.480
<i>I'm doing this myself.</i>

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:22.280
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:28.460
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:35.000
I was prepared for the time you left

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:41.840
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:48.350
After I embraced you with all I had

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:57.900
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.570
filled my heart

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:08.080
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:14.750
You gave me happiness

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:18.090
Until I meet you again one day

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.590
Until I know what you are truly like

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.140
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.810
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:28.930
I won't forget your smile

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.620
<i>The last place I went with Shimao...</i>

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:55.590
<i>I thought seeing this view alone would make me cry,</i>

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.130
<i>but surprisingly, almost disappointingly, I'm fine.</i>

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.430
<i>Is it because this place is nice</i>

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.390
<i>or because it's a good match for me?</i>

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.140
<i>That tree...</i>

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.400
<i>It seems so kind.</i>

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.650
So trees that look easy to climb seem kind?

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:25.910
Don't you think so?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.950
I don't know.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.080
I never thought about it.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:30.910
For example,

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.420
this thick branch is like extending its arm in a friendly way

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:40.670
and the branches up there look so inviting it's like they're saying, "Go ahead, have a seat."

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.880
I'm sure this tree is friendly toward people.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:47.140
Where did you get that notion, Rokka?

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:47.930
From a picture book?

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:52.480
Maybe it's from reading a story a long time ago, about a woman who loved trees.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.270
What is that book?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.850
What happens at the end?

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.980
The woman is reborn as a root.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:58.820
Why?

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:04.650
The tree that was loved by the woman found itself wanting to impress her,

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.660
and just kept growing.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.700
So it became a tall tree and got older.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.210
The woman lived next to the tree all that time,

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.960
but when she was 3000 years old, the roots of the tree became sick.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.750
She wanted to cure the tree so badly

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.300
that she ate a root

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.550
and died from its poison.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:30.810
But she was reborn as part of that root, so it's a happy ending.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.060
The woman dies?

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.310
Well, she ate poison.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.100
That's a happy ending?

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.070
After all, she did get to become a root of the tree.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.570
That's an exceedingly silly story.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.570
Who's the author?

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:45.440
My mother.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.570
She wrote it?

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.870
When I was in elementary school,

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:54.700
making picture books out of cloth was a popular activity among my mother and her circle of volleyball friends.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.250
I don't see what that has to do with volleyball.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.880
Come to think of it, that's a pretty heavy theme for something made out of patchwork.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.340
I loved that book.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.260
What's the title?

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:07.970
I forget.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.010
You forget?

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.760
That's how much you like it?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.430
If possible,

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.480
I wish I could

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.360
eat all of your bad cells, Shimao...

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.610
You'd get an upset stomach.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.110
Or rather, they'd metastasize.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.410
Shouldn't you take off your backpack first?

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.240
Catch!

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.330
Yeesh...

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.170
I was right, this tree is kind.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.210
Come on up, Shimao.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.540
There's no way.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.550
Coward!

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.670
Sticks and stones.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.420
You're a wild one, Rokka.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.390
A tomboy, huh?

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.010
You never learned as a boy?

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:53.680
Learned what?

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.350
How to climb a tree. In P.E.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.890
What they teach kids out in the mountains...

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:59.230
So city kids aren't taught that in class?

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:01.770
I wouldn't know.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.110
I never took part in P.E.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:06.360
Not even once?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.490
Nope.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.990
Nobody ever passed the baton to me in a relay or anything.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.660
Poor little Clara, never getting to go outside and play.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.290
<i>The first time I saw Shimao's lack of coordination,</i>

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.630
<i>I thought he was just messing around.</i>

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.460
Miss!

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:28.510
Your change!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.720
You've forgotten your change!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.550
What a strange way to run.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:39.770
<i>This low hill that also serves as a course for elementary school excursions</i>

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:45.310
<i>is the highest peak on Earth that Shimao ever climbed.</i>

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.150
<i>Stepping firmly on the soft ground,</i>

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.240
<i>looking up at the sky...</i>

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.320
I want to be a cicada in my next life.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.620
I should've brought tools with me.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:02.540
That way, while we were walking, I could've gathered all the flowers you point at

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.250
and made them into an impromptu bouquet.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:09.090
Next time, let's bring a sponge too, so we can have a flower exhibition by the river.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.140
<i>The promises we couldn't follow through on</i>

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.350
<i>were like the number of stars, quietly overlapping.</i>

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.190
<i>When I die,</i>

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.110
<i>will you eat a little bit of my bones?</i>

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:33.860
<i>I didn't fulfill my promise either.</i>

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.120
What this time?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.670
No swallow, huh?

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.960
I... haven't become a frog or anything.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.670
I'd hate to become a character like that.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.600
I've seen this before somewhere.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.390
Another fairy tale.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:04.140
I mean, these are all stories I read a long time ago.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.190
What are you doing, old man?

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.650
Who're you calling old?!

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:10.860
Any way you look at it, you're an old man.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:11.280
I can't hear you!

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.990
Don't judge a man by his size!

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.320
Okay, okay, don't get mad.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.070
I don't blame him. I mean, we <i>are</i> tiny.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:19.580
You see where I'm coming from?

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.330
Hello there!

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.290
Hello.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.080
We're busy right now!

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.040
We don't have time to bother with you!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:27.830
See you later!

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.630
Let's take a little break! I'm tired!

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.920
Come on, let's go!

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.300
You're gonna carry that glass coffin, right?

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.050
I can't hear you!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.640
If you know the answer, don't ask.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:40.930
The princess is sleeping.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.930
She's gorgeous sleeping like this, too...

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:43.970
That's pretty rude!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.430
I want to take a break, too!
That's pretty rude!

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.020
No surprise, this is a nonsensical world, too.
I want to take a break, too!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:47.600
No surprise, this is a nonsensical world, too.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:49.480
What was that?! We're all serious!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.270
Serious! Determined!

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.070
Can I check something?

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:59.410
Can I play the prince who wakes the princess up with a kiss?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:14.960
Of course not!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.340
But the old men just...

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.430
Those twerps.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.520
You're not the prince.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.310
I told you before, don't shoot me down with that expression on your face.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:31.190
I love you.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.280
That's funny!

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.240
Don't tease me!

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.200
Woe is me...

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:38.820
Huh?

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.530
You've got a bright future ahead of you. You're young, and honest.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.370
You have everything the prince doesn't.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.830
What bright future?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.580
You're full of hope, right?

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:53.590
Aren't you supposed to say that kind of thing when the future is wide open?

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.590
In these circumstances, I can't see anything.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.670
You're healthier than the prince, right?

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.220
Is that really such an advantage?

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.720
From the point of view of someone who didn't possess it since childhood.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.730
Yeah, but even so, will it do me any good?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.100
You have a future.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.190
But the manager won't have eyes for me.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.780
Even so...

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.070
I love who I love.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.380
<i>Who is it?</i>

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.590
<i>The person planting my Snow-in-Summer...</i>

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:46.850
<i>is who?</i>

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.560
<i>Who's digging up that gravestone without permission?</i>

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:55.860
<i>Umm...</i>

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.860
<i>The owner of that old trowel...</i>

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.380
Shimao?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.420
It <i>is</i> you, isn't it?

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:24.720
Hey.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.890
Can you hear me?

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.690
<i>He's not turning around.</i>

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.270
<i>Is it because he's Shimao?</i>

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.940
<i>Or is it because he's Hazuki?</i>

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.740
<i>I don't believe it.</i>

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.990
<i>That strange way of running.</i>

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.580
Hey.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:54.830
What are you doing?!

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:58.040
Dummy! You dummy! Idiot! Dumbass!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.340
You're gonna fall if you keep running like that.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.760
Wait! Even if you run, you can't get away!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:13.980
That's right.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:16.810
I love her.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.120
<i>From the beginning,</i>

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.540
<i>it was like lightning crashing down</i>

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.290
<i>until he couldn't move anymore.</i>

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.040
<i>And all I could do was watch.</i>

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.550
<i>His dry palms.</i>

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:47.840
<i>The flower arrangements like crashing emotions that clashed with his nonchalant demeanor.</i>

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.930
<i>I've been chasing after them</i>

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.720
<i>all this time.</i>

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.060
Shimao,

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.060
you like using flowers with strong colors, huh?

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:03.030
I analyzed that myself a long time ago.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.570
Is there a reason?

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.780
Certainly, I do have a tendency to use vivid red and orange colors.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:12.030
Well, it may be simple,

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.580
but maybe I use flowers that are easy to avoid at hospital visits.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:23.840
<i>I don't know how self-aware he was about it,</i>

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.420
<i>but like clockwork, right before he was hospitalized,</i>

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:33.850
<i>he would always use vitamin-colored flowers so bright you could barely look at them.</i>

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:38.190
<i>As if warding off a curse, he would turn the whole house into a garden</i>

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:40.560
<i>and then head for the hospital.</i>

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.110
<i>Arrangements are like mirrors.</i>

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.200
<i>Shocking pink for sheer vexation.</i>

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:50.820
Honest to a fault.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.700
<b>Notification of Divorce</b>

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.830
I already stamped my part.
<b>Notification of Divorce</b>

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.080
<b>Notification of Divorce</b>

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.370
In case something happens, I thought we'd better do everything we can
<b>Notification of Divorce</b>

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:02.500
while we still have the chance.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.880
I mentioned it to my sister, too,

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.010
but depending on circumstances,

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:14.600
you can sell the store at your own discretion.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:20.850
<i>No matter how many lies easily come out of your mouth,</i>

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.860
<i>you can't fool me with those hands that work with grass and dirt.</i>

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.400
<i>Both the shop and garden</i>

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.860
<i>are always overflowing with your love.</i>

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.580
<i>The strangely-shaped vase singled out at a flea market,</i>

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.330
<i>the rice bowl you bought for 100 yen, serving as a makeshift pot...</i>

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.630
<i>Your emotions welling up, like snow falling and lying thick on the ground.</i>

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:53.050
<i>The shop runs over with those unique, unrivaled treasures,</i>

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.060
<i>so leaving the job of throwing them away to someone else is just too heartless.</i>

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.230
Even if you made someone else decide,

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.650
you'd just be making them get lost in a maze.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:07.520
Besides,

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.240
I don't know how I would part with it.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:14.820
This sounds unfair,

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.450
but I don't think I have the right to choose.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.620
If I could choose,

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.340
my vote would be to stay with you until I'm a decrepit old man.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:30.340
But if that's impossible,

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:36.140
you're the only one who's able to dispose of all of my things, Rokka.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.890
So all I can do is entrust you

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.190
with throwing them away.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.810
It's really pathetic, I know...

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:53.400
I have to throw away everything?

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:55.990
Even though

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.410
I'll start to forget one day?

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.410
But I still have to?

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.420
<i>Everything Shimao made,</i>

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.630
<i>everything he chose.</i>

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:12.210
...loved.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:13.220
<i>All of it,
...loved.</i>

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:15.180
...loved.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.180
<i>I absolutely...
...loved.</i>

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.180
...loved.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:21.810
This...

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:25.940
All of this...

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.440
They're Shimao's personal belongings.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:35.150
You smell like mothballs from head to toe.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:00.800
You're Shimao,

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:03.640
aren't you?

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:12.940
Tell me...

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.030
How long?

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:24.830
How?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.640
Say something!

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.980
D-Don't cry.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:32.560
Please,

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.150
Rokka.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.330
Shimao!

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.670
Yes.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:24.860
<i>I didn't mean for it to go this far.</i>

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:32.620
<i>The idea was to bury part of my bones on this mountain,</i>

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.830
<i>then surrender everything.</i>

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.420
<i>If I break my promise here,</i>

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:42.300
<i>it'll feel like I'm even more of a scoundrel.</i>

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:45.050
<i>But I</i>

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:50.470
<i>was a bastard from the moment I wasn't able to come back to life.</i>

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:54.810
<i>It's like</i>

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.480
<i>I'm too late</i>

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.400
<i>with lots of things.</i>

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:01.990
It's kind of late to notice this,

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.820
but there aren't any insects here?

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:06.870
Drawing each one would probably be a pain, wouldn't it?

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.080
So that's what it is.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:12.040
Right? Prince...

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:16.330
Why are you suddenly acknowledging me as the prince?

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:26.430
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:32.180
you always smile

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:36.270
Tell me why

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:40.150
it won't go away

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:41.940
I gave you everything

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:43.780
You gave me anything

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:48.570
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:50.240
still my everything

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:53.450
I love you

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:56.830
It is a miracle

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.960
like fleeting snow

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:05.920
that fell in summer

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:12.930
If I hadn't met you

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:16.140
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:23.650
and nothing would have pressed down on my chest

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:29.320
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:36.370
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.500
When I close my eyes

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:45.510
you're right beside me
